Hi,

Can I work on this?

I took a look at this. It seems:
In case of Handler: `WorkflowExecutionExecpetion` -> `e.getFailure()` -> details preserved
In case of Validator: `WorkflowExecutionException` -> `execeptionToFailure(e)` -> gets reserialized -> original details are lost

The execptionToFailure:

```java
@Nonnull
  default Failure exceptionToFailure(@Nonnull Throwable throwable) {
    Preconditions.checkNotNull(throwable, "throwable");
    return new DefaultFailureConverter().exceptionToFailure(throwable, this);
  }

// the above calls:
@Nonnull
  @SuppressWarnings("deprecation") // Continue to check operation id for history compatibility
  private Failure exceptionToFailure(Throwable throwable) {
    // ....
    if (throwable instanceof ApplicationFailure) {
      ApplicationFailure ae = (ApplicationFailure) throwable;
      ApplicationFailureInfo.Builder info =
          ApplicationFailureInfo.newBuilder()
              .setType(ae.getType())
              .setNonRetryable(ae.isNonRetryable());
      Optional<Payloads> details = ((EncodedValues) ae.getDetails()).toPayloads();
      if (details.isPresent()) {
        info.setDetails(details.get());
      }
      if (ae.getNextRetryDelay() != null) {
        info.setNextRetryDelay(ProtobufTimeUtils.toProtoDuration(ae.getNextRetryDelay()));
      }
      if (ae.getCategory() != null) {
        info.setCategory(FailureUtils.categoryToProto(ae.getCategory()));
      }
      failure.setApplicationFailureInfo(info);
    } else if (throwable instanceof TimeoutFailure) {
      // ...
    return failure.build();
  }

```

Even though there is a case for `ApplicationFailure`, what actually happens is:
`Validator` ---throws---> `ApplicationFailure` ---stored inside as `Failure`---> `WorkflowExecutionException`
then `SyncWorkflow` catches is as a generic `Execption`, so this is what actually gets passed to `exceptionToFailure()` and the above case is never triggered.

## A Possible Fix?

In `SyncWorkflow` in handleUpdate:
```java
@Override
  public void handleUpdate(
      String updateName,
      String updateId,
      Optional<Payloads> input,
      long eventId,
      Header header,
      UpdateProtocolCallback callbacks) {
    final UpdateInfo updateInfo = new UpdateInfoImpl(updateName, updateId);
    runner.executeInWorkflowThread(
        // ...
              try {
                // ...
              } catch (ReadOnlyException r) {
                // Rethrow instead on rejecting the update to fail the WFT
                throw r;
              } 
              // Add this ...
              catch (WorkflowExecutionException wee) { // use e.getFailure() here } 
              // Before generic Execption
              catch (Exception e) { ... }
              // ...
  }
```
